  "authority_invariants": [
    "Realtime/conversational frontend never selects a concrete backend model/provider",
    "provider override is per-turn and never mutates Conversation Core default provider",
    "unsupported action/memory/current-data/background-task work never falls through to model-generated fake success",
    "Electron/React remains a thin client; Jarvis Core remains authoritative",
    "Realtime Mini/Cedar/WebRTC, backend providers, wake providers, and future capability handlers remain replaceable",
    "desktop route ownership is resolved in a forced text-only function response before any audible response; final spoken responses have tools disabled",
    "every desktop turn prints an explicit route owner; Core Call logs occur only for Core-owned routes and share the route call_id/turn correlation",
    "development terminal conversation trace is observational only; user voice transcription never drives routing or response authority",
    "background/durable execution routes to long_task even when the work is also an external action",
    "gate-free A/B is allowed only when all external tools and Core delegation are disabled",
    "text-only tool probe never forwards function calls to execution bridge; fake outputs always indicate executed=false",
    "tool-probe VAD speech_started/stopped use shared turn handler; provider text/tool outputs remain intercepted; real tools forbidden"
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Memory 2.0 capability handler is not implemented yet",
    "permissioned action/tool handler is not implemented yet",
    "current-data lookup capability is not implemented yet",
    "durable background task worker is not implemented yet",
    "strong backend model route is opt-in and requires a separately validated model ID in local configuration",
    "initial hard-reasoning routing policy is deterministic and local rather than model-classified",
    "direct desktop turns still include a silent cloud routing inference; 50-100 ms should not be assumed until a non-sequential/local fast path is validated",
    "development voice conversation tracing uses a separate asynchronous ASR stream and should be disabled in production unless explicitly required",
    "Repair6 parallel shadow is a measurement experiment only; it does not lower first-audio latency or output speculative audio.",
    "Fast direct-only A/B disables actions/Core/sleep; tool-capable gate removal still needs a pre-audio publication guard",
    "tool selection probe is text-only; Luna and real actions are intentionally not executed and voice timing is not benchmarked",
    "live tool-capable voice without a router requires audio publication gate not built here",
    "Tool-probe VAD regression was fixed structurally but awaits provider/WIndows live acceptance"
  ],
